**Program Design:**

1. We will use a simple trial division algorithm to generate prime numbers. This algorithm works by iterating from 2 to the square root of each candidate number and checking if it is divisible. If it is not divisible, the number is prime.
2. We will use a boolean array to keep track of whether each number is prime or not.
3. We will use a list to store the prime numbers.
4. We will use a loop to iterate from 2 to the desired limit (100) and add prime numbers to the list.

